From 374bc444693defb9e53ada46352d5265bd86a81f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 09:23:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [AGS] Add a small fixed-voice PCM mixer for DOS (Sound
 milestone S1)

mojoAL/SDL2_sound stay gated out on DOS (patches 0005/0006) -- rather
than port either for DJGPP, PLAN.md's Sound milestone plan decided to
replace them: a small fixed-voice mixer on one SDL3 audio stream at
Tier-2 (11025 Hz mono S16), matching doskutsu/dossage's own established
default and dossage's own 0039 lesson (convert once at load, mix as
add-and-clip -- no per-chunk resampling).

This patch adds the mixer module standalone (platform/dos/
dos_audio_mixer.h/.cpp): 8 voices (3 reserved + 5, matching AGS's own
SCHAN_SPEECH/SCHAN_AMBIENT/SCHAN_MUSIC reservation), each a plain
append/consume PCM ring capped at 32 KB; dos_audio_mixer_pump() tops up
the shared SDL3 stream to a ~186ms target depth (a top-up, not a
run-to-cap fill, per the hub's docs/audio.md convention) and services
the DOS SB ring via the shared SDL_DOSAudioPump(); an underrun counter
(a pump cycle where an ACTIVE voice had nothing to mix, not merely an
idle mixer) and a compact status-string builder for the
audio_vital_status vocabulary PLAN.md's Sound milestone defines
(pcm=<device>@<rate><ch><bits>,voices=<n>,underruns=<n>;midi=<backend>).

Nothing calls this yet -- wired into audio_core/openalsource/sys_main in
a later patch, once the WAV/VOC loader (also a separate patch) exists
for it to consume. This patch is independently buildable: the two new
files compile and link cleanly, inert until referenced.
